@startuml Admin_Roles_Management_SSD

actor "Super Admin" as SuperAdmin
actor "Regular Admin" as RegularAdmin
participant "UI: User Roles" as UI
participant "Database" as DB

== View User Roles ==

SuperAdmin -> UI: Access user roles management
activate UI

UI -> DB: Fetch all users
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return users list
deactivate DB

UI -> DB: Fetch current admin info\n(check if Super Admin)
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return current user info
deactivate DB

UI --> SuperAdmin: Display users table\n(with editable role dropdown)
deactivate UI

note right of SuperAdmin
  **Super Admins:**
  • aaronbagain@gmail.com
  • sophiamikhaela.fabian.cics@ust.edu.ph
  • juander714@gmail.com
end note

== Super Admin: Change User Role ==

SuperAdmin -> UI: Select new role from dropdown\n(tourist ↔ admin)
activate UI

UI --> SuperAdmin: Show confirmation dialog
SuperAdmin -> UI: Confirm role change

UI -> DB: Update user role
activate DB
DB --> UI: Role updated
deactivate DB

UI -> DB: Log admin action
activate DB
deactivate DB

UI --> SuperAdmin: Show success, refresh list
deactivate UI

== Super Admin: Delete User ==

SuperAdmin -> UI: Click "Delete" button
activate UI

UI --> SuperAdmin: Show warning dialog\n"This action cannot be undone"
SuperAdmin -> UI: Confirm delete

UI -> DB: Remove user record
activate DB
DB --> UI: User deleted
deactivate DB

UI --> SuperAdmin: Show success, refresh list
deactivate UI

== Regular Admin: View Only ==

RegularAdmin -> UI: Access user roles management
activate UI

UI -> DB: Fetch all users
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return users list
deactivate DB

UI -> DB: Fetch current admin info\n(check if Super Admin)
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return current user info\n(Not Super Admin)
deactivate DB

UI --> RegularAdmin: Display users table\n(with disabled dropdown - View only)
deactivate UI

note right of RegularAdmin
  **Regular Admin Restrictions:**
  • Can view all users
  • Cannot change roles
  • Cannot delete users
  • Role dropdown is disabled
end note

== Search and Sort ==

SuperAdmin -> UI: Enter search term or sort column
activate UI

UI -> UI: Filter users by:\n- Name, email, role\nSort by any column

UI --> SuperAdmin: Display filtered/sorted results
deactivate UI

@enduml
